WEBVTT

00:05.250 --> 00:12.450
Have an important question for you why are you pursuing the PMP.

00:12.640 --> 00:14.840
Why do you want to be a PMP.

00:15.190 --> 00:19.290
What's it going to bring to you is that an ambition.

00:19.460 --> 00:23.680
It's going to make you a better project manager sort of financial reward.

00:23.680 --> 00:26.310
So why are you doing the PMP.

00:26.350 --> 00:30.010
Well we're talking about benefits in this section.

00:30.010 --> 00:36.400
So what benefits will the PMP bring to you and to your organization and your customers.

00:36.430 --> 00:42.070
So what want you to make a connection here between the PMP it's a test it's a very tough challenging

00:42.070 --> 00:42.870
test.

00:42.930 --> 00:46.420
It's a lots of terms to know a lot of information to know.

00:46.570 --> 00:53.790
But how is that going to make you a better person not just a project manager but a better person.

00:53.860 --> 00:58.470
I think it gives you confidence in your life that you've overcome a challenge in that.

00:58.570 --> 00:59.860
That's great.

00:59.860 --> 01:02.650
It's a realization of ambition.

01:02.710 --> 01:09.580
It is the ability for others to put trust and confidence in you because obviously you've done the work.

01:09.610 --> 01:15.570
You have experience and you have insight into the generally accepted practices of project management.

01:15.760 --> 01:17.070
So those are all benefits.

01:17.080 --> 01:22.130
But what other benefits might you have somebody that takes some time and think about that like how is

01:22.130 --> 01:25.120
this really benefiting me as an individual.

01:25.360 --> 01:30.850
You know for me it's opened up a lot of doors and created opportunity but it also helped me become a

01:30.850 --> 01:37.060
better project manager to think more about just getting from A to B but to think about getting from

01:37.060 --> 01:40.910
A to B to C to D all the way to the end.

01:40.980 --> 01:44.260
There's a lot more moving parts and components.

01:44.320 --> 01:50.520
So over the years as a project manager you know we learn it's not always the shortest route.

01:50.560 --> 01:57.190
Sometimes we have to accommodate stakeholders and accommodate politics and other factors that can really

01:57.190 --> 01:58.880
seem to interrupt our project.

01:58.960 --> 02:02.060
Well the truth is that's part of project management.

02:02.110 --> 02:06.880
So I want you to think about the benefits as to what is this going to do in your career and in your

02:06.880 --> 02:08.130
life.

02:08.140 --> 02:08.700
All right.

02:08.920 --> 02:11.470
You're doing great you're making great progress.

02:11.500 --> 02:12.240
Keep it up.

02:12.460 --> 02:13.810
I'll see you in the next lecture.
